      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I agree it's quite cluttered up close. I try to avoid large instances, but when I end up in one it's always extremely claustrophobic to have that many nameplates. This functionality is already available via the earmuff mode (annoyingly)(bias), but requires earmuff to be enabled, so there's clear demonstration of capability to do this already with the caveat of not being a separate feature. Separating this ability from the feature that is already built in (earmuff) would both add this functionality and improve upon the feature that is already available.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-02-28T03:49:20.247Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I'm not sure how this would best be implemented, but for small spaces with a lot of people like clubs, it would be nice to have a way to have nameplates only visible for people close by to you. Maybe something based on the earmuffs mode?\n\nI often want to see the name of the person I'm talking to if someone comes up to me and says hi, but in crowded areas, too many nameplates can be distracting and visually noisy, and not having to open the quick menu to see nameplates quickly would be nice (especially given they take a moment to appear).\n\nThis stands out especially for worlds that have gimmicks that mess with depth, which can break culling (such as okgold's newest world - https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_12613486-24b7-41da-b070-07e5ddc8a3d7), or when viewing crowds from above as per the screenshot attached (which has both issues)\n\nWorlds like this look better without nameplates, but when sitting on the sidelines I'd like to be able to see the nameplates of the people I'm talking to.\n\nMaking the nameplates smaller or less opaque does not help in this sort of case, there's too much going on.",
